d voice, to the constable, " I'll not a very sober character, have mistaken his excited skin ye alive when I come out." condition for drunkenness. Silver-street, MILITAILY CAsitS.—James Donnoland, of S. . Mr. Swift applied for Costs, urging that the police a deserter from the 2nd Lancasbire Regiment, stationed and not the justices were really the respondents. Til2 at Salford, was sent to Strangeways to await an escort,. Bench refused costs.</p>
        <p>FOOTB ALL.</p>
        <p>•„'' Secretaries of Football Clubs are requested to note that reports of matches played on Saturday must be sent to the head office. Bewsey-street. Warrington, not later than ten o'clock on Wednesday morning.</p>
        <p>GEO. G. BIISSEY &amp; CO. are leading Makers of Foot Balls. Hockey, Golf. La Crosse, and requisites for Sports, Gaines and Gymnasia. Catalogue may be had on appli• cation to the Sports Manufactory, Peckham Eye, S.B. Trade f ECD(C Mark.</p>
