      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1893-01-21_WidnesExaminer_art0089" n="art0089">
        <head>NATIONALIST CONVENTION AT NAVA N.</head>
        <p>NATIONALIST CONVENTION AT NAVA N.</p>
        <p>SELECTION:JOF CANDIDATES ;FOR7,NORTHI AND MISOUTH MEATH. A Nationalist Convention, called for the purpose of selecting candidates to contest the two divisions of county Meath at the approaching election, were held on Tuesday at Navan, under the presidency of Mr. W. O'Brien,W.P. The other members of Parliament who attended were Messrs. D. Sheehy, P. G. Kennedy, D. Kilbride, M. Austin, Jasper Tully, J. C. Flynn, P. A. Chance, and P. M'Donnell. Most of the party had been in the county previously, and arrived in the town by different routes. There was no interference of ally kind on the part of the Parnellites beyond some shouts of "Fire to your heels and toes," an expression which, haying been more than once referred to during the hear- ing at Meath election petitions, has become quite a stock phrase with the Parnellites. The Convention was numerously attended, 60 Roman Catholic clergymen being present. The proceedings at the start were pri• Tate, and resulted in the selection of Mr. Jeremiah Jordan, who before the general election sat for one of the divisions of Clare, as a candidate for South Meath, and Mr. James Gibney, a native of county Meath, for North Meath.</p>
